      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-21T00:23:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t see any reason to enable it only for one but not the other- that seems like a very easy way to cause feature drift where things get fixed for only one board in general, and seems to suggest that we want to put a \"don\u0027t touch this file\" notice in prj.conf and make it policy to only adjust boards individually.",
      "parentUuid": "fa993d35_6e68f81f",
      "revId": "ce36b8852c4029623df384433a5c632d53ebb817",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0ec2927f_5d20b551",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1281040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-21T00:27:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Understand, and originally I did have config in this file, but it got a bit confusing to have it spread over 2 files, and also the other boards such as corsola keep this file empty (and that was the example I was suggested to follow).\nIt sounds good to put a comment in prj.conf indicating that no config should be present and to use the board specific config.",
      "parentUuid": "10ccc8da_80b82431",
      "revId": "ce36b8852c4029623df384433a5c632d53ebb817",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0be14ac8_2a27d7ec",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1361259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-21T00:55:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "While it may be easier right now to have one file, I think it\u0027ll be worse in the long run when a nereid config file appears, because then every change to config needs to remember to update both, even if somebody is only working on one board (or specifically call out that it applies to that one board): it would be very difficult to tell if a given change is correct or not, whereas having the shared configuration makes intent obvious.",
      "parentUuid": "0ec2927f_5d20b551",
      "revId": "ce36b8852c4029623df384433a5c632d53ebb817",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "984d1f2c_55110b76",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1281040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-21T01:07:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So corsola is the pattern we\u0027re following here, and I would much prefer not to deviate too much from that pattern until we are more confident about the best approach to sharing config.\nThe question does arise about how much to make common - keeping them completely separate at this stage does remove any ambiguity or possibility of impacting the other board when making changes to a board.\nSo at this stage let\u0027s keep them separate, and when we have final configs for both we can properly consider what should be common (e.g I don\u0027t think any of the bringup options like this one should be common anyway).",
      "parentUuid": "0be14ac8_2a27d7ec",
      "revId": "ce36b8852c4029623df384433a5c632d53ebb817",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
